{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/306030-necro-what-did-the-original-trinity-lines-get-wrong-and-what-did-they-get-right","id":306030,"title":"[Necro] What did the original Trinity lines get wrong, and what did they get right?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-07T12:09:43-08:00","id":306030,"title":"[Necro] What did the original Trinity lines get wrong, and what did they get right?","content":"I own all the digital copies available from DrivethruRPG for all three lines of the original Trinity universe. Unfortunately, I have not had time to read them, but that has changed and I'm going to dive in and give them a proper read through. Since I'm not overly familiar with the lines despite being a fan, and I prefer my landmines to have warning labels, I'm going to ask the boards two questions:<br /> <br /> What did the original Trinity lines get wrong?<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> What did they get right?<br /> <br /> Mechanics, setting details, characters, wording, chapter organization, the works; what were the foul balls, and what were the home runs?<br /> <br /> (Obviously, this is going to be based on subjective opinion, so I ask that the conversation be kept civil.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 11-07-2014, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T13:09:34-08:00","id":306071,"title":"","content":"Talking about mechanics, Aberrant had a neat scaling system where the presence of damage adds and armor adds would cancel each other out... and then failed to use it in a manner which might balance some of the combat issues that cropped up. The most obvious problem was that while Mega-Strength soared to incredibly heights of damage, Mega-Stamina gave regular soak, and not much of it in comparison. You'd need several Enhancements just to be able to survive a Mega-Strength punch... whereas if Mega-Stamina had provided an armor add, it would have put everything back to super-strong wailing on super-tough as if the two were relatively normal combatants.<br /> <br /> The division of Brawl and Martial Arts was also troublesome, most notably because it took a stance of &quot;Brawl = European, Martial Arts = Asian&quot; with one lone exception for savate. Of course, giving a broad envelope term like Martial Arts to an unarmed combat Ability is also problematic. By the time you get to one being fit under Strength and the other under Dexterity, the mechanical issues have taken a backseat to the entire concept of trying to mess with unarmed combat in this manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T19:44:29-08:00","id":307102,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input, Saur Ops, and...<br /> <br /> ...good grief, this branch of the forums is <i>quiet</i>. I guess there just isn't much to talk about right now, is there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T08:14:45-08:00","id":307444,"title":"","content":"Hey Prometheus878, <br /> <br /> I think there's a few lurkers, and a bit of discussion from time to time but yeah, without anything all that tangible yet to discuss it gets a little quiet here. It'll pick up though, probably around the time when Open Dev starts - which various hints suggest the end of the year (nothing official on that, just hints).<br /> <br /> I guess you asked a fairly broad question about editions about to be replaced as well, which might be why you're not getting much traction. <br /> <br /> I can give you a fairly broad answer, though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The three different game lines are all very different, but what stands out to me the most is that certainly Aeon (Trinity) and Aberrant read &amp; play like products of their time. As mentioned in other threads on this forum the broad themes, representation of signature characters, metaplot nature and certainly game mechanics are <i>very</i> 1990's. Not that this is <b>all</b> bad (I happen to enjoy the metaplot of Aeon, actually)...... but gaming has moved on since the games were published the better part of 20 years ago. <br /> <br /> We've cribbed a bunch of stuff from this forum, rpg.net and so on covering what we (think we) know so far about the reboot over here: <a href=\"http://bit.ly/1xbTHvz\" target=\"_blank\">http://bit.ly/1xbTHvz</a><br /> <br /> From what you've read of the 1st editions, and what's been pulled together at that link, is there any changes being hinted at that stand out to you as good / bad ideas or that highlight what you see as good / bad things in the 1st editions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T18:17:32-08:00","id":307705,"title":"","content":"All of the stuff in there is gangbusters. Two in particular stand out to me though:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(discussing the writers' &quot;World of Brightness&quot; tag for the Continuum) &quot;World of Brightness&quot; doesn't mean nothing bad ever happens. I mean, that would probably be a pretty boring setting for gaming in, yeah? But like...yeah, Aeon is in some ways a postapocalyptic setting. But the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">post</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> part of that is what's important. It's a world that's recovering. A world that's looking to the future with hope and sacrifice and unity, with characters who are invested in actively making things better. There are threats, and some of them are scary and powerful, but there's a real sense of &quot;we can make it through this into something better if we all work together.&quot; And that's before we get into stuff like Aeon assuming that the Aberrant War happened but Aberrant not having to go that way at all due to quantum-wantum timey-wimey stuff. (</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#1155cc\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u><a href=\"http://goo.gl/PR2SkL\" target=\"_blank\">http://goo.gl/PR2SkL</a></u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">)</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Good on them! We already have World of Darkness, let's have some good ol' idealism where the heroes are capital H Heroes. I assume The Trinity Universe never got as bad as WOD, but I'm still seeing some stuff that makes me scratch my head.<br /> <br /> For instance: &quot;The Aeon organization was founded by a heroic idealist, but that sort of thing is just plain <i>old fashioned</i>; <b>Ruthless Pragmatism</b> is the <i>modern</i> thing to do. <i>Obviously</i>, the best way to protect the world is by backstabbing several thousand superhumans, even though they're creating a new golden age and we might need their help against any space aliens or dimensional monsters that would threaten humanity. <i>Obviously</i>.&quot; &quot;Uh, sir-&quot; &quot;<b>PRAGMATISM</b>!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> Really, Project Utopia? Really?<br /> <br /> On that subject:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(Discussing the Aeon Trinity\u2019s portrayal in the TU, and the black mark Aberrant\u2019s Proteus left) I think this will be less of an issue with the new game(s), since one of the big directives is that the Aeon Society/Foundation/Covenant/Trinity/whatever </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">is not sinister.</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Like in big bold block text THESE ARE THE GOOD GUYS. (</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#1155cc\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u><a href=\"http://goo.gl/vHlq3f\" target=\"_blank\">http://goo.gl/vHlq3f</a></u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">)</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Yes! Not everything has to turn to muck over time! Here's hoping this will address the above criticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T18:33:18-08:00","id":307712,"title":"","content":"A concept that really hits the right notes for me in 1E Aberrant is Taint. Not sure about the name, but I like what it is and I like how it works; definitely one of the better representations of &quot;power for a price&quot; I've seen in RPGs. Easy separation of good guys and bad guys: bad guys are the ones who have given up on their Humanity. Even if I were to run the system without the setting, I would still keep the Taint mechanics in there, as the threat of rampant mutation is just too good a plot point to pass up on.<br /> <br /> &quot;Alright, I've drawn up my character, and... he's not <i>quite</i> as capable as I would like. Hm... ya'know, these low-level Taint mutations aren't <i>too</i> bad. In fact, some of them are pretty cool! Multicolor hair? Count me in!&quot;<br /> <br /> --- Several Sessions Later ---<br /> <br /> &quot;OH MY GOD I'M A MONSTER!!!! AHHHHHH!!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> Priceless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T22:34:06-08:00","id":308862,"title":"","content":"Well, there\u2019s definitely room in Aberrant for the X-Men \u2014 superhumans for whom their powers are as much curses as blessings. Superheroes are a diverse bunch, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T01:07:26-08:00","id":308894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/306030-necro-what-did-the-original-trinity-lines-get-wrong-and-what-did-they-get-right?p=307705#post307705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good on them! We already have World of Darkness, let's have some good ol' idealism where the heroes are capital H Heroes. I assume The Trinity Universe never got as bad as WOD, but I'm still seeing some stuff that makes me scratch my head.<br /> <br /> For instance: &quot;The Aeon organization was founded by a heroic idealist, but that sort of thing is just plain <i>old fashioned</i>; <b>Ruthless Pragmatism</b> is the <i>modern</i> thing to do. <i>Obviously</i>, the best way to protect the world is by backstabbing several thousand superhumans, even though they're creating a new golden age and we might need their help against any space aliens or dimensional monsters that would threaten humanity. <i>Obviously</i>.&quot; &quot;Uh, sir-&quot; &quot;<b>PRAGMATISM</b>!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> Really, Project Utopia? Really?</div> </div> </div> </div>At least one of the 1e Trinity writers, Bruce Baugh, has gone on record with his dislike of what Aberrant did with the Aeon organisation, seeing it as a waste of potential.<br /> <br /> (To my mind, the TU writers didn't seem to have a clear idea of Aeon's place in the setting until Adventure!, with it being a protagonist group - although to be fair, the original Aeon/Trinity was done in a rush, taking 10 months from conception to publication, and on top of that had a first-time developer.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T06:29:13-08:00","id":309036,"title":"","content":"I like gritty and dark as much as anybody but that's what the world of darkness is for. As far as I'm concern injecting realism and consequences in a superhero setting doesn't necessarily make it darker, it can still be positive and optimistic, in certain ways it even becomes more humane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T03:41:06-08:00","id":312857,"title":"","content":"I absolutely love most of the sci-fi setting of Trinity. My biggest two beefs were: 1. No real info on India. India will be a major power in the decades to come, and was specifically stated as such in game. More info would be helpful. 2. Africa is magically a single country. I don't necessarily like the idea of continent wide super states happening. Look at the trouble the EU is having. Africa is much larger, much more diverse and has different problems than Europe. I would support the idea of a first world Africa no problem, but I think some more political variation would have kept it more interesting. Also, not enough Africa info!<br /> Aberrant was great, but I always felt the metaplot got in the way. I wanted a near future super hero game. That's what I played, but I ignored metaplot. Love the game though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T18:03:36-08:00","id":313379,"title":"","content":"There's been plenty of hints that Onyx Path are approaching non-western cultures with a bit more.....um....refinement this time around in Aeon (Trinity). I'm looking forward to seeing how that is handled too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T22:21:14-08:00","id":314227,"title":"","content":"It is possible that India and Africa had little information because they were the home areas of the two Orders that were &quot;missing&quot; in the main book. They might have intended to bring out the Order and area information in a later supplement and never got around to it (though the teleporters book they did bring out was rather lacking on information on Africa and concentrated on space instead). As Marin mentioned the Trinity stuff seemed a bit rushed, it also seemed a bit handwavy and forced too at times though overall it was a good game in play.<br /> <br /> A nice thing with the original Aberrant is that like other White Wolf games character generation and gameplay were faster and easier to keep flowing than most other superhero games of the time on a mechanics level though the metaplot did not lend itself well to the mainline style superhero genre. I heard the game mechanics would fall apart at higher experience levels but never actually ran into the problem; coming from Champions everyone made rather complex builds that were versatile but did not advance very quickly. I am looking forward to the new stuff too, I hope it will be as agile as the old version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","user":"BC001","date":". 11-17-2014, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T22:53:43-08:00","id":314275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BC001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/306030-necro-what-did-the-original-trinity-lines-get-wrong-and-what-did-they-get-right?p=314227#post314227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is possible that India and Africa had little information because they were the home areas of the two Orders that were &quot;missing&quot; in the main book. They might have intended to bring out the Order and area information in a later supplement and never got around to it (though the teleporters book they did bring out was rather lacking on information on Africa and concentrated on space instead). As Marin mentioned the Trinity stuff seemed a bit rushed, it also seemed a bit handwavy and forced too at times though overall it was a good game in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a plan for an Africa book, Bright Continent, but the line got cancelled. My vague memory's saying it would've been a setting book absent an Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T09:54:35-08:00","id":314644,"title":"","content":"Bright Continent was planned to have a new &quot;psi order,&quot; composed of the exiles and rejects of the other orders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T10:15:28-08:00","id":314668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/306030-necro-what-did-the-original-trinity-lines-get-wrong-and-what-did-they-get-right?p=314644#post314644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bright Continent was planned to have a new &quot;psi order,&quot; composed of the exiles and rejects of the other orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such a rag-tag bunch of misfits would've easily eclipsed the other Orders in terms of PC appeal, so maybe it's a...bright spot...that the book never came out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T16:56:28-08:00","id":314937,"title":"","content":"I'm just looking for an Africa that's somewhere between Shadowrun's hand waived &quot;Tribal Lands&quot; and Trinity's hand waived &quot;United Aftican Nations&quot;. Now a ruined Europe and corporate fascist North America were great! I would have liked to see the telepath order not be a Chinese government agency, plus more Asia info! Basically a more realistic and fully realized political situation. Rembrandt the core book mentioned a &quot;Turkic Federation&quot;, a magical hand waived union of Turkey and Central Asia? I was about 15 at the time but I was like &quot;what the hell?&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T23:13:19-08:00","id":315090,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that we're talking about a version of Earth about a century into the future that's experienced a war between superhumans and regular humanity that only ended in mundane humanity's favor because we said &quot;get the hell off our planet or we take you with us.&quot; Knowing full well the sorts of crap that a <i>regular</i> war will force countries to ally over, I'm kinda wondering where you draw the line on 'hand waved.' Why does an openly-fascist version of North America that has not taken over the Psi Order within its own borders make more sense than a future Chinese government that has? I'm not trying to be snarky or rhetorical, I'm just having trouble with your logic and wouldn't mind a little clarification there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T06:34:28-08:00","id":315348,"title":"","content":"Oh you're fine! I don't think that ANY of the psi orders should be part of a government. I think psi order/government conflict is good for the setting, and making them part of a government always sat funny with me. More a personal style choice than anything else.<br /> In the end, I could have accepted the UAN had I known more about it, probably. Just with what was released, it seemed a bit hand waived. <br /> I get the idea of a post superhuman war situation creating new political realities, but the only real unification to come from WW2 is the EU, which took forever to form and is still having trouble finding itself, IMO. So alliances yes, political unions between countries that don't necessarially have common interests, history or culture are just a bit harder for me to swallow without explaination.<br /> <br /> I'm sure whatever the team puts out I will love though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T08:48:46-08:00","id":316324,"title":"","content":"As for the Turkic Federation.... I was in Turkey a couple of years ago and there is definitely the sentiment behind that in place in the here and now. Turkey sees itself as a rising power and sees any nations (or parts of other nations) as part of what should be their sphere of influence. With a few events going a couple of ways, I could easily see something like this happening in this world, much less a world where the conflict with novas would have caused the kind of chaos that drives nations, ethnicities, etc. to throw in together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T22:30:21-08:00","id":316954,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the info! Good to know there are elements in Turkey that would support that. <br /> Turkey may want that, but what about Central Asia? Anyone have a line on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T13:51:20-08:00","id":317684,"title":"","content":"As far as the Turks (of Turkey) are concerned, they think the Turkic speaking countries are all on board. Or should be. Or will be once it all gets started. A lot of the Central Asian countries speak Turkic languages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T18:46:35-08:00","id":317856,"title":"","content":"Yeah but speaking a language in the same family doesn't meant anything. Heck, the Central Asian countries are divided on the freaking alphabet they should use.<br /> <br /> Anyways, enough derailing. My bad!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T08:06:26-08:00","id":332966,"title":"","content":"Pre Script: I finally got the document to load, while much of it agrees with what i'm driving at, it seems most of the setting is already done - so I doubt anything i say will inspire any detail changes, much less changes in overall tone. I suppose we just wait for more information now.<br /> ...<br /> <br /> Most of this will concern the general meta-plot and mood of the Aeonverse, apologies if that isn't up for discussion here, i'm not able to get the referenced document for some reason...<br /> <br /> Meta-Plot and Mood<br /> I'm not entirely convinced white washing the Aeon society is what is called for in a reboot - the complexity of the Aeon society through history made Max Mercer one of the most intriguingly understated characters i've had the pleasure of trying to unravel. On one side we have an idealistic two-fisted detective who fits seamlessly into a pulp adventure setting, on another we have a father of lies not unlike the Watchmen's Adrian &quot;Ozymandias&quot; Veidt, who makes a centralized earth for a costly greater good (or pure hubris, depending on how you land on the character). The two variations being neither confirmed or denied in the setting left a lot of leeway for ST interpretation (e.g. my brother and i run the Aeonverse two different ways, they both work uninterrupted by the none-the-less rich setting info).<br /> You would vindicate my brother and invalidate me by cleaning it up too much in that regard, so i have a little skin in the game there.<br /> I'm having difficulty finding the mission statement quoted in earlier posts, so i can't comment on other subjects therein. While i won't deny the thriving hopes of the Trinity settings, a &quot;world of brightness&quot; isn't really what i got out of the series. It reads more like Clive Cussler than Sax Rohmer, more like Watchmen than Justice League and more like Revelation Space than Star Trek. The chilling question on the Aeon societies silence during the second world war, the intriguing absenses of Max from the timeline (i suspect he managed to hide from the society sometimes despite his presence, or simply take another identity) and the heavy inference of the society falling apart after WWII, if only briefly, all point to a grey-scale setting with many of the trappings of popular fiction.<br /> The setting was built for deconstruction, FTL &amp; Psionics comes with a price, super powers come with a price, and, if you would indulge me, i always considered Adventure to be leading into a ridiculous, silver-age, Venture Brothers meets Top Ten era during the fifties and sixties as the first hammersmith effect weakened. This history was of course covered in great detail by the society, but like their pulp-flavored periodicals of earlier times - nobody really believed them and the tales were swept under the rug by the society in an attempt to regain dwindling credibility as the inspired people places and things slowly began to power down prior to the N-Day effect created by Mal as a kind of love letter to the Hammersmith era. In other words; a price is paid there too in my own head-canon.<br /> To clear it up, i'm not arguing for a darkening of the setting - i'm rather arguing for it's vast genre to not be pruned back in the name of contrasting your other books. Trinity can stand alone - it has done for a long time. The Aeon society is a mirror for the society of the times and as such must grow and make mistakes with the people they serve - i feel the single unbroken society as singularly evil or good would feel out of place and overly simplified in the otherwise complex setting material, the real story of the Aeon society is likely more complex than it seems. Project Rewrite hints at this.<br /> In conclusion, please don't take the Gothic elements of storytelling out of this setting - the skeletons in the closets, the secrets, horrors and mystery of the loose threads are an important part of what makes the setting so compelling. It isn't the world of darkness, but neither is it the world of brightness - instead it's something in between, with extensions reaching into both extremes - it can be bigger than light and dark.<br /> <br /> Aeon/Trinity 2120<br /> I agree with the other posters lamenting the lack of detail for the UAN, who otherwise fill an important role vacated by the U.S. and (to a lesser extent) my own nation of Australia as a developing new nation upon which the world can hang its progressive dreams. Further, the handwaving nature of collecting africa into a single entity without exception (outside of the middle east at least) suffers from western-centric generalization, a flaw the setting could do with shedding as much as possible.<br /> Some fairly extensive works (India Underground, Asia Ascendant, etc..) were never truly canonized in the setting either, which was sad, considering the amount of thought that went into them. The story of Nippon in particular helped to fill the blanks between Aberrant and Trinity, the controlled utopia of China is an important element as well from that book.<br /> In other areas, i wondered at the reasoning, game-wise to cut up the Op-Net into much more nationalized subnets? It seems very strange from a 2014 perspective, what was the difference betweeen the internet and opnet anyway? Bandwidth? Compression algorithms? Handshake protocols? It smelled of needless rebranding and despite it working fine in game, it <i>is</i> showing it's age. I actually like the individual national server hubs, leaves a lot of room for ST's to play about - i played with the idea of some old central-asian servers under loose Russian federation control had been left as-is since Kuwasha's death and still carried a patial echo of the IT nova - a maimed digital version of Warfire in western Europe, but otherwise the region had security levels comparable to the internet we know and love today. The idea of needing physical access to important cables at the hub also made for a fun bit of espionage play for those without electrokinesis. Underground, pirate internet protocols being illegal was delectably Orwellian too. I just think a better technical reason for the change would be appreciated.<br /> Finally (for now), the shocking alieness of Trinity era Aberrants created an immense amount of inspiration for this Storyteller, i could pull ideas straight out of lovecraftian horror or victorian ghost stories and isolate groups in deep space while fending off these threats. What i'm saying is that Taint was a great storytelling tool in combination with the semi-magical Novas in a relatively hard science setting - the worst monsters were once us.<br /> And the biggest threat we've encountered so far is some no-name, the Colony. What are some of the 'prime threats' like so far in the future? The imagination swoons with possibility.<br /> <b>Right</b>: A whole heap, mostly decent futurism, unparralleled scope in combination with the rest of the Aeonverse, No Faster than light travel (violated by the coalition eventually, but in an acceptably dramatic manner), Non-US centric (now expand the worldview even more for extra points), completely inhuman aliens, few explicit bad guys and more sympathetic illustrations of them hidden just below the surface, intrigue aplenty, hopeful depictions of space travel with sufficient dystopia to keep it interesting, corporate dominance, manipulative media and PR muddled subtexts to nearly everything, Eden, Khantze Lu Ge, Process 418 (cyclical conclusion), QK purge (India Underground made the subtext clearer, not sure if that was the intent when written)... Just a wonderful, inspiring game. My favorite, in fact.<br /> <b>Wrong</b>: PSUEDO GRAVITY (hard science please), Opnet Protocols (okay, but what's the difference?), not enough Transhumanism (Nova-tech AI, neural uploading of personalities to emulators, cyborgs, spacers with enough implants to walk in vacuum naked, uplifted animals, etc...), not enough focus on the solar system worlds (including moons), too much focus on the Psi Orders (telegraphing the meta-plot much?), no good 'gotcha' moment for the Upeo's return (i know the bright continent and star-crossed were building to something, but we never got the payoff), same with the Doyen. Actually a lot of what's wrong with the 2120's setting is that it just wasn't finished... Let's adress that going forward. -smile-<br /> <br /> Aberrant 2008<br /> I never ran Aberrant in its setting, the Novas i ran were in the 2120's. But my brother ran many games in the setting - in his inimitable silver-age style - throwing a deconstructionist bone my way once or twice a game, but never letting that darkness consume his vision of the setting. Proteus was his main tool in this excercise - although they may seem contradictory or even offensive to the super-heroic feel of the game - reconstructing the genre's assumptions to <i>exclude</i> those possibilities would be folly, in my humble opinion. Many decry the darkening of comics, but there <i>are</i> stories to tell there - see Rising Stars, Powers and any number of other modern deconstructions of the genre.<br /> I think the main issue may be the reproductive one - as anyone should be able to sympathise with humanity wanting to protect itself from the nova age, but even then i can't imagine the fertility depression would last forever and a few Novas would be immune by nature/anima. The Aeon society may not have seen this N-Day stuff coming - the realisms of Time Travel being left up to each individual ST, and the effect was created by Primoris/Mal, who at the time, given what we know, was likely a terrifying enemy of the society after their battle in 1943 (again, the subtle silence on WWII leaves a lot of room for interpretation here). Over-reaction by Project Proteus is partly where the Teragen draws their grey-scale mojo from. My brother uses the Teragen as unrepentant super-villains - but i see a whole lot more potential there - why should humans have dominion over a population of superior beings? They aren't looking for dominion over humans only themselves (at least not in the excerpts of the Null Manifesto that we are given), it's very Brotherhood of Mutants and potentially sympathetic - see Synapse 'defending' the Opnet to the best of his abilities in the war. Devolving Mal from Primoris into a kind of comic-book villain seems such a waste of the details given in the books, like writing Magneto to rob a bank just for the money and not for some much grander scheme born from his own torment.<br /> I ran low-quantum Novas in two different campaigns in the 2120 setting and found enough references in the Trinity books to do so - it would have been lovely to see those kind of tangible threads in Aberrant from Adventure! Where is Sarah Gettel's legacy? What mark did the Ubiquitous Dragon leave on his Orient homeland? Who/Where is Michael Mercer? (I heard the d20 books adressed the last one with Margaret, but still)<br /> Otherwise, my main issue with Aberrant would be the inevitable arms war that occurs at higher levels of physical conflict - Mega-Strength 5+ must be accounted for by all characters wanting to join a fray, Quickness keeps stacking every time you buy it, etc... But i'm going to stay away form sytem discussion otherwise, because i feel i'm a little out of my league having experience in only a dozen or so systems under my belt, most of which old/obsolete by now. Just don't base it off MMO mechanics if possible - they are two different types of gaming, thanks.<br /> <b>Right</b>: Intrigue, comic-like superheroes (i like the deconstruction, but they need to be there for me to do that), Media infatuation (N! network still feels relevant in 2014), dubious power structures (Proteus, DeVries, Directive), morally grey factions (in some interpretations, but a Storyteller system strength at the time), sillyness (silver-age stuff can actually work despite the shadowy background), heroics (not just comic book stuff either, some of the Novas of 2008 and earlier are earnest heroes with a whole world rallying against them, despite the cameras and fans - see the Fireman), information contrast (the bright colored and shallow setting material against the intriguing depths of less obvious machinations) and the meta-plot war (the text takes on new meaning in combination with the history given in 2120).<br /> <b>Wrong</b>: Not enough tie ins with Adventure!, Obvious trolling by Proteus (more subtlety would have been nice), eventual arms war between players and ST (in my experience), lack of balance with the other games in the Aeonverse (sucks to be them, it can work, but anyone who isn't a full quantum Nova is going to feel left out and underpowered, taint be damned), investment in characters who either turn against earth, go insane or both without known exception, even the Nihonjin remnants are falling apart by 2120.<br /> <br /> Adventure! 1922<br /> While both my brother and i have played about with crossing over with the Adventure game, neither of us have run a game in the setting - thus disqualifying me from any experienced input. But i mentioned my own head-canon about the time between and the Hammersmith effect repeats in 2122/2123 which makes me interested in the meta-plot. I bought the book to answer some of my questions about Max, Primoris and other history. Now days, my brother and i take turns coming up with silver-age nonsense to explain why the likes of Danger Ace, Whitley Styles and Sarah Gettel can suddenly appear at any time in any genre with a smart comment loaded and followed by world-tilting Deus Ex Machina in the wake of their astronomical inspiration. Given Taint and the Doyen, it just seems natural that the era of Adventure! was mostly blind to the ripples their telluric manipulations were causing - however subconscious. But that was when the society was at it's most innocent - it's clear that something BAD happened inbetween this society and the one we see so little of in the following era - but the trinity era once more has some of this hope back - perhaps co-inciding with a more stable return of Max Mercer prior and after process 418.<br /> No rights and Wrongs here, i haven't enough experience with the game for that, just the setting material. But the inventions system needed to be in all the books, as did a lot of what was detailed, like background mastery, dramatic editing (as a sidebar, i agree) and a final call on whether Daredevils were a third type of inspired or what everyone who wasn't inspired could become would be useful for the Quantum/Noetic framework.<br /> <br /> I have a lot of topics to read through, but i'll come back and try to find the document referenced earlier for a bit more more input. Apologies for the long-windedness, it's been too long and i'm a little overwhelmed by all i have to say on the subject as a huge fan and a long time participant in this shared universe.<br /> If you made it all the way through, you regain willpower and earn an experience point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Got the document to load and added a pre-script note. 12-07-2014, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T14:31:10-08:00","id":336303,"title":"","content":"They never would have had uniforms as cool as PsiCorps... uh, I mean the Ministry's.<br /> <br /> - C.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Clayton A. Oliver | Formerly Ubiquitous<br /> <br /> <i>When the half-light starts to rise/And the long gone come back again<br /> After the shortcuts and the highs/Comes the pain<br /> And the rain</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2966-tegyrius","name":"Tegyrius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T05:58:03-08:00","id":338000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tegyrius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/306030-necro-what-did-the-original-trinity-lines-get-wrong-and-what-did-they-get-right?p=336303#post336303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They never would have had uniforms as cool as PsiCorps... uh, I mean the Ministry's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh.<br /> <br /> Don't worry, I promise I'll never tell my players who to blame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T01:00:06-08:00","id":361073,"title":"","content":"I read the whole thing about the UAN (I am South-African) and automatically went <i>WTF</i> I know the &quot;dark continent&quot; seems an impenetrable mess of violence and poverty but that is not the overall case. As a group we debated the likely future of Africa in light of Aberrant and came to the conclusion that there would be more a commonwealth of nations rather than a federation, after all we can look at the EU to see why becoming too closely integrated - especially economically - is a terrible idea. A political union is likely but it would not be terribly close beyond immediate borders. Even a century into the future even with an influx of folks from the west due to the Aberrant War a transplanted USA into Africa would only work in a dreamworld. Africa will be its own distinctly african thing, with all the good and bad that entails. No stranger than anywhere else on earth but nearly as xenophobic (overall) as presented in Trinity in this century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Man's unfailing capacity to believe what he prefers to be true rather than what the evidence shows to be likely and possible has always astounded me. We long for a caring Universe which will save us from our childish mistakes, and in the face of mountains of evidence to the contrary we will pin all our hopes on the slimmest of doubts. God has not been proven not to exist, therefore he must exist.</i> <b>--Academician Prokhor Zakharov</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3246-galaxy-master-zhad","name":"Galaxy Master Zhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T22:30:00-08:00","id":368299,"title":"","content":"It's hard to say Aeon got much right; I loved the game for the setting more than for the mechanics. Still, it did innovate some of the features that would later become standard in Storyteller/Storytelling, like standardized target numbers, auto-soak, and matching a skill to an attribute.<br /> <br /> Aberrant was actually one of my favorite systems because of the tiers of powers made there costs very easy to remember: 1, 3, or 5 nova points. Simple. You had enough points to muck about with, certainly, but I never felt overwhelmed. Taint also worked out okay for the mechanic. I wasn't fond of the power modifiers found in the player's guide, as I've seen those things in superhero games and I think they cause more problems than they solve - you bloat the power entry, you slow down character creation, you don't get any greater guarantee of balance than if you had just made a new power whole-cloth, and you turn getting the power you want into this cruel minigame that you can fail. No thanks.<br /> <br /> Adventure was brilliant - it just needed more stuff. More knacks of all types really, as I felt painfully limited in a nearly limitless setting. Invention was great though, as was dramatic editing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T22:32:14-08:00","id":368301,"title":"","content":"Probably the biggest setting mistake is just how very much Aeon is in the background, when it is meant as a unifying element. Whitewashing or not I feel a number of players who liked the game didn't even really understand Aeon's role or what they were about or how they had any kind of authority in these weird mutant ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T20:44:06-08:00","id":373284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Galaxy Master Zhad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/306030-necro-what-did-the-original-trinity-lines-get-wrong-and-what-did-they-get-right?p=361073#post361073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read the whole thing about the UAN (I am South-African) and automatically went <i>WTF</i> I know the &amp;quot;dark continent&amp;quot; seems an impenetrable mess of violence and poverty but that is not the overall case. As a group we debated the likely future of Africa in light of Aberrant and came to the conclusion that there would be more a commonwealth of nations rather than a federation, after all we can look at the EU to see why becoming too closely integrated - especially economically - is a terrible idea. A political union is likely but it would not be terribly close beyond immediate borders. Even a century into the future even with an influx of folks from the west due to the Aberrant War a transplanted USA into Africa would only work in a dreamworld. Africa will be its own distinctly african thing, with all the good and bad that entails. No stranger than anywhere else on earth but nearly as xenophobic (overall) as presented in Trinity in this century.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey just so you know, I didn't want to come across as implying that Africa can't or shouldn't unify. I just rejected it because the official explanation was big war = Africa suddenly unifying with no explanation. Europe is having enough trouble integrating and Africa is even more diverse in terms of wealth, culture, language and national identity. So more info could make it ok if the unification was handled in a non hand waving way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T09:27:11-08:00","id":379083,"title":"","content":"Hi there, it seems that most agree that the 90\u00b4s have passed and especially Trinity needs to steer away USA-Eurocentric worldview.<br /> The setting has a tripolar setting with China, Subsaharan-Africa and Brazil/Sudamerica as &quot;The Big 3&quot;<br /> <br /> As written by other above, Event though Europe &amp; USA are described as former shadows of themselves, they take to much space in the old core.<br /> <br /> I generally liked the orders, for me the Docs, ISRA and the Ministry were the most intriguing ones. Orgotek was too much of an order that almost appeared like a Mary-Sue. (Almost singlehandedly building the jumpships).<br /> <br /> I actually liked that the technology level was not to cyberpunky - except for the Nihonjin. Who are the masters of hardtech and secret wetware. And alien Biotech which is not understood completly which makes for a nice cringe factor.<br /> <br /> Ofcourse there is need for a technological update regarding computing and 3-D-printing.<br /> But the Kuwasa-OpNet-Wipeout was a very good narative to explain the slowed down technological advancement.<br /> The chaos afterwards made a new paranoid net and almost no further scientific exchange as we are used too.<br /> <br /> I would more lampshade that most of nowadays orbital/spacetechnology are actually nova-age artifacts. Which is okay for explaining highly efficient energy cells and grav-crystals but less nanobot technology or even actual A.I.<br /> <br /> I actually would favour an rule upgrade to the revised storytellersystem, as I don\u00b4t know this Scion-System. But I actually like cinematic rule sets. I would also include in the new core rules all psion powers &amp; modi with reference which is normally thaught and which are secret modes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T22:17:41-07:00","id":888843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/306030-necro-what-did-the-original-trinity-lines-get-wrong-and-what-did-they-get-right?p=317856#post317856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but speaking a language in the same family doesn't meant anything. Heck, the Central Asian countries are divided on the freaking alphabet they should use.<br /> <br /> Anyways, enough derailing. My bad!</div> </div> </div> </div>Chewy, those are pretty valid doubts, no problem with bringing it up, quite the contrary in fact, i would say.<br /> <br /> And language can be a funny thing, it can mean nothing or serve as a springboard for cultural identity/identification, literary romanticism and much nationalistic hoopla. Stuff like pan-slavism or bolivarian propaganda rearing its head can serve as current examples of a far from unique phenomena. Anyway, a number of countries in central asia have common elements in strong turkic cultural-linguistic roots - and domination/oppresion by the Russian/Soviet imperialism during a good part of 19th-20th centuries. While their current relations with Russia are quite friendly, it could certainly be turned upon its head depending on the vagaries of decades and politics, Yugoslavia making a bitter example of a group of people united in a common cause &amp; identity that incrementaly smoldered toward implosion, hard, in the decades from World War I to the end of the Cold War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T21:01:12-07:00","id":889618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/306030-necro-what-did-the-original-trinity-lines-get-wrong-and-what-did-they-get-right?p=888843#post888843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And language can be a funny thing, it can mean nothing or serve as a springboard for cultural identity/identification, literary romanticism and much nationalistic hoopla. Stuff like pan-slavism or bolivarian propaganda rearing its head can serve as current examples of a far from unique phenomena. Anyway, a number of countries in central asia have common elements in strong turkic cultural-linguistic roots - and domination/oppresion by the Russian/Soviet imperialism during a good part of 19th-20th centuries. While their current relations with Russia are quite friendly, it could certainly be turned upon its head depending on the vagaries of decades and politics, Yugoslavia making a bitter example of a group of people united in a common cause &amp; identity that incrementaly smoldered toward implosion, hard, in the decades from World War I to the end of the Cold War.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude! What are you smokin'! First of all, necroin' really old threads? Then commenting with some sort of existential linguistic analysis?! I'll admit, I am quite inebriated as I write this, but damn! I feel like I need a PhD in archaic languages or a good number of hits on some prime ganja to keep up with you! At least I was entertained!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There is no good or evil. There is only instinct corrupted by intelligence.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","name":"KingOfDreams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T21:53:20-07:00","id":889646,"title":"","content":"I'm the first to admit that while entertained with reading stuff in threads i'm all to frequently will forget to check the damn dates before posting. Either that or i'm too much of a Hollowfaust (from Scarred Lands) fan to be too bothered over necromancy. About a PhD, it might be the inebriation talking, as i haven't even finished my degree history yet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though i do admit to possibly hopping madly between places and periods in trying to explain the context behind a Turkic Federation in Central Asia, what can certainly be confusing to follow. But then history can be something of a hot mess of random stuff happening or repeating itself at times, anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T15:52:26-07:00","id":909545,"title":"","content":"Have not had a chance to read through the whole read. I'll do once I get home tonight or on anothe break. I have the most experience with Aberrant and it was the first &quot;super hero&quot; based RPG I played. So I have a huge love for the game.<br /> <br /> As far as what they got right. <br /> At the time they system was amazing. The severity of powers was staggering and wonderful. Also, as a setting of the real world with super powers mixed in was ground breaking for me. <br /> They nail the feel of average person gets into situation X and gets powers. So you have some Novas that work for Microsoft and others that say screw it I'll be a super powered mercinary. Even some that are the best secretary you could ever ask for. A lot of the Novas are self centered and use their ability a for some degree of profit. They even have a story of one guy that is immune to disease and absorbed radiation who gets a job as a lab tech because he does not have to wear an environmental suit. The powers have a good scaling however there are some consistency issues.<br /> <br /> What they got wrong:<br /> I'll start this an state that this is from my perspective and play style. <br /> Where the taint system is amazing for showing the slow fall of a god linking it to the only source of aberrations was a mistake. If you wanted to play a beast or night crawler character or anyone with a none super human aperence of fitness model then you had to taint your character through the roof. Beast by the system would have at permanent taint of 6 or so. Body hair, skin color, eyes, ears/teeth, hands feet. No aberrations show up till the third dot of taint or fourth. So your walking very close to the pit to make a non human looking character.<br /> Where mega-strength is powerful and mega-stamina is under powered in comprising you can stack M-Stanima, armor, force field, immunity and any other soak power. Look at Iron Skin Andy Vance. He is designed as a soak machine. This added to when a nova reaches Q 6 and slaps the first mastery onto any non M-Strength damage power it quickly outstrips M-strength damage capability. Even if you add in crusher. <br /> There is also some inconsistency with the power level of level three technics vs the second level power they are pulled from. Where the level 3 power has more versatility the inconsistency, decrease in range, kph, area and added cost becomes out stripped again. So there needs to be a bit of balance there brought back in. Not hard to do. <br /> Extras, needs some work there as well. I've been using a system where you can have a number of extras equal to rating in the power. Each extra you want to use coast 1 extra quantum on activation. This allows for costomization and diversity without always needing to push the power, and possibly failing to get enough successes, and gives you a lot more reason to have more then the first dot.<br /> Speaking of first dot. With most powers very little ultimately changes after the first dot. Flights speed is a nominal increase, hyper movement is much better and Q-Bolt is so so. So having the extras = to dot rating is a great reason for players to push for higher ratings. <br /> There are others and I have a document I've been working on of home brews. Such as M-Strength getting more damage as it goes higher vs the 5 per dot. M-Stan dropping a lot more health levels on you as it goes up and the extras. <br /> <br /> All in all it is still an amazing game! I'm very excited for the 2e!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T12:19:23-07:00","id":930464,"title":"","content":"Well, since that thread seems to have reopened...<img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>The things they did get right:</b><br /> The Atmosphere, it was and still is just awesome. The whole premise of gods walking among earth is great, hell even the psions get their fair share... and suspicious looks.<br /> <br /> Aeon as an organization was quite good, but it could have been better... although the fact that Aeon/Trinity was cut short didn't help in that matter. I do and still LOVE the fact that there were LOTS of skeletons in their closets.<br /> Their lies and very actions led to the Aberrant War and probably pushed a good number of them over the brink, them imprisoning and experimenting on them, basically sterilizing them and doing all kinds of black ops against the homo novus as a whole, while at the same time coating themselves in a aura of sheer benevolence... that had guts.<br /> <br /> The Quin were awesome. I loved the Icon suits, the fact that they were slug like and not humanoid and that they had to rely on humans for FTL.<br /> They were technologically superior to mankind, but at least one house of them wanted to ascend in their politics by making deals with the humans.<br /> I loved that story, also the fact that they had really, really nasty house politics... and freakishly strong biotech.<br /> That they had reasons to interact with mankind at all, due to their obvious shortcomings, that was quite brilliant.<br /> The best thing about them was that all of them were psionics, but that they had already reached the end of their potential and they knew it.<br /> They had reasons to fear humanity and they had reasons to work with them, yet it was never clear cut... which lead to a deliciously complicated political game.<br /> <br /> <b>The things they did get wrong:</b><br /> Well.. I did hate the Quantum and Psi pools from the very beginning.<br /> If I play those games I do so because I don't WANT to bother with resource conservation.<br /> Seriously, some powers could drain an Aberrant in no time, which was NOT fun.<br /> Psions had it even worse, they were limited to short bursts of using their psionic powers.<br /> In both cases, I did find that thematically not fitting. I just threw that part out and never looked back.<br /> Having the ability to use their abilities whenever they liked was way better for creativity and storytelling purposes, in my opinion at least.<br /> <br /> The Chitra Bhanu (aka the Chibs or &quot;Dark Psions&quot;), those were order that was a bit squandered.<br /> I did like their backstory, how they did fall and India Underground cleared up some other issues.<br /> In any case what I did not like was the fact that their powers were so limited.<br /> I would have preferred it greatly if they would have been some kind of mini novas/aberrants, being capable of acquiring their psionic powers AND being forced or capable to pick up Mega-Attributes or Nova powers the further they develop their psionic potential. Thematically it would have been a great fit AND it would have explained how ONE or at best TWO Dhiren were capable of picking off Aberrants and dragging them back to the clinic.<br /> Them being capable of basically &quot;merging&quot; psionic and nova powers would also explain why the Doyen where so interested in them, while at the same so scared that they had the orders crush them. Hell, they even went so far as engineering public opinion against the Chibs, which can't have been an easy feat given the fact that the Proxies were around.<br /> <br /> Which leads to the Doyen. Thematically they were great, BUT their actions were at best haphazardly revealed... and almost never prone for players to discover.<br /> This led to a certain amount of disconnect when it came down to them... so much so, that I outright put that part of the story on the table for my players.<br /> <br /> <b>What I would want to see in a new edition:</b><br /> More Transhumanist elements<br /> More advanced tech<br /> Quantum and psionic power systems which are as freeform as possible<br /> Keeping the grey areas and conspiracies which were awesome to work with, a definite and marked in difference between full blown psionics and novas,<br /> Chitra Bhanu who as an order learn to late that their path sets them up to be kinda hybrids between novas and psions... thus another reason why only so few belong to their order<br /> Another one for the Chitra Bhanu, that more survive the purge... if that goes down like it did in the first edition.<br /> An Aeon that has still to fight with governments about where it can go and what it can do... and still has enough political clout to make things happen and has to resort to black ops when there are no other options.<br /> Cut down Del Fuego a bit, he had basically all cards in his hands and had even a good chunk of Chibs working for him... it seemed a bit much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9298-bhurano","name":"Bhurano","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:43:28-07:00","id":1065996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/306030-necro-what-did-the-original-trinity-lines-get-wrong-and-what-did-they-get-right?p=306071#post306071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking about mechanics, Aberrant had a neat scaling system where the presence of damage adds and armor adds would cancel each other out... and then failed to use it in a manner which might balance some of the combat issues that cropped up. The most obvious problem was that while Mega-Strength soared to incredibly heights of damage, Mega-Stamina gave regular soak, and not much of it in comparison. You'd need several Enhancements just to be able to survive a Mega-Strength punch... whereas if Mega-Stamina had provided an armor add, it would have put everything back to super-strong wailing on super-tough as if the two were relatively normal combatants.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't really find that in some years of playing. The thing was, soak was additive The only thing that added to Mega-strength was claws. That topped out at +30 as I remember.<br /> <br /> Soak on the other hand... You could have Eufibre 5, Armor, Invulnerability, Mega-stamina with Resilience, Absorption (Feeding into Invulnerability of course), Force-field (nicely cumulative with Mega-stamina) and probably a few more I've forgotten. All stacking. As I emember it you could easily surpass the Mega-strength damage with soak, and for a lower amount of points.<br /> <br /> One issue with Aberrant was the XP costs. It was normally far better to buy a Mega-dot than buying more dots in a power, and raising a normal attribute high just didn't pay. Get someone with a maths background to look it over this time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:59:12-07:00","id":1066044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/306030-necro-what-did-the-original-trinity-lines-get-wrong-and-what-did-they-get-right?p=1065996#post1065996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't really find that in some years of playing. The thing was, soak was additive The only thing that added to Mega-strength was claws. That topped out at +30 as I remember.<br /> <br /> Soak on the other hand... You could have Eufibre 5, Armor, Invulnerability, Mega-stamina with Resilience, Absorption (Feeding into Invulnerability of course), Force-field (nicely cumulative with Mega-stamina) and probably a few more I've forgotten. All stacking. As I emember it you could easily surpass the Mega-strength damage with soak, and for a lower amount of points.</div> </div> </div> </div>25 successes for five mega-dots = 15 nova points, not counting the cost of raising Quantum to 4. Force Field could match it with fewer dots, but it was a big could, because unless you got the fixed version of the power, you were only really guaranteed your Quantum in soak - you get .9 successes per Mega-Stamina dot rolled and .5 for each normal Stamina + Force Field die, so on average, say, Force Field 2 and Mega-Stamina 3, with Stamina 5, means 12.4 soak plus Quantum; rounding down to 12 + Quantum, in this case a minimum of 2 for an expected bonus soak rating of only 14 from FF, for a total soak of 20L/25B. Also, right away, getting more dots in both M-Stamina and in Force Field, you're getting into the territory of spending about as many, if not more, nova points on defense that were spent on offense, and possibly coming up short. Armor and Invulnerability could get even more costly, especially if you wanted a broad category for the latter.<br /> <br /> Also, adding onto this was the Crush enhancement for M-Strength, which could theoretically bump the 25 auto-successes to that plus however many qps you could spend per turn according to your node rating. That, however, was not something that got in until the errata came into play with the player's guide. Since it is an enhancement, however, that means that you can pick it up with your M-Strength purchase at no additional cost.<br /> <br /> All in all, lots of experiences are liable to be different, but the math is what it is, and the powers could have done with some serious restructuring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One issue with Aberrant was the XP costs. It was normally far better to buy a Mega-dot than buying more dots in a power, and raising a normal attribute high just didn't pay. Get someone with a maths background to look it over this time. </div> </div> </div>Well, you had to boost up baseline Attributes and Quantum in order to buy Mega-Attributes up higher, since the ceilings were the lower of your baseline Attribute value and (Quantum + 1). I think there might have been some harsh intentions there expecting you to buy up baseline traits with your starting np allotment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T21:56:23-07:00","id":1066702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/306030-necro-what-did-the-original-trinity-lines-get-wrong-and-what-did-they-get-right?p=308894#post308894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At least one of the 1e Trinity writers, Bruce Baugh, has gone on record with his dislike of what Aberrant did with the Aeon organisation, seeing it as a waste of potential.<br /> <br /> (To my mind, the TU writers didn't seem to have a clear idea of Aeon's place in the setting until Adventure!, with it being a protagonist group - although to be fair, the original Aeon/Trinity was done in a rush, taking 10 months from conception to publication, and on top of that had a first-time developer.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's something deeper in tonal difference between Aberrant and the other games. Part of it is &quot;ESB&quot;-effect, where middle chapters are structurally going to be down notes, but I think someone's political philosophy was in play as well. Aeon/Trinity had a New Deal theme of people working together to build a better world. Aberrant strongly suggests that type of &quot;Utopianism&quot; is not to be trusted, and it's individual freedom from collective institutions that needs to be paramount. I'm not saying the writers were full on pro-Teragen, it's supremacism was a negative. But there was a very libertarian fear of institutions and people wanting to prioritize making change for the greater good rather than leaving you alone going on.<br /> <br /> I think it's notable that someone also went and made a Libertarian President of the US. It lines up with someone's wish fulfillment going on.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong - I'm not saying games should be apolitical or they need to perfectly line up with my politics. I'm just saying there was an incongruency between Aberrant's politics and the politics of the other games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T13:47:51-07:00","id":1069593,"title":"","content":"My single biggest problem with Aberrant was that each of the developers very clearly had a favorite &quot;pet&quot; faction that they wanted the game to revolve around - Hatch with the Aberrants; Blackwelder with the Teragen - and rigged everything about the setting in their favor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T13:48:25-07:00","id":1070841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/306030-necro-what-did-the-original-trinity-lines-get-wrong-and-what-did-they-get-right#post306030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did the original Trinity lines get wrong? What did they get right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I own every single Trinity book, including the original black AEON hardcover. Love the game to pieces, and looking very much forward to backing the new Kickstarter. Hope they can get more of the original giants back as writers to back up Ian's vision. I'm only a happy amateur regarding Ab and Ad so I'll leave those other games out for now.<br /> <br /> <b>As for my thoughts on what Trinity got right:</b><br /> + The Psi Orders<br /> + Fantastic metaplot<br /> + BioTech<br /> + Agents<br /> + Really great take on how the world would look 100 years from now. Frighteningly so. Many things are coming true.<br /> + Inverted many cyberpunk tropes<br /> + Aliens (Qin, Doyen, etc.)<br /> <br /> <b>What Trinity got wrong:</b><br /> X Unbalanced psi in the Core<br /> X Complicated &amp; clunky freeform psi in the Player's Guide<br /> X Good core rules, but many unclear &amp; clunky side systems<br /> X Alien Encounter 2 was a wasted opportunity<br /> <br /> I disagree with the sentiment that the setting is too 90's, although I generally agree with CHILL's comments. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Trinity wasn't grounded in the well-meaning idealism of how things &quot;should be if we could just balance historical wrongs&quot;, but rather a rather impressive &quot;what could it look like if current trends spiral?&quot; brand of speculative fiction based on the global trends at the time. After having spent 5+ years in the US and 5+ years working in China, and seeing the global developments over the last 20 years, it is shocking to me how precognizant the original writers were. Both geopolitically and technically. Not perfect, but far better than any other sci-fi game I can think of released 10-20 years ago.<br /> <br /> I look forward to an updated, daring, and bold take on where the world will be in 2020. All in all, I am super-enthusiastic about the new edition. Really like the new system being proposed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5621-wintermute","user":"Wintermute","date":". 03-30-2017, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5621-wintermute","name":"Wintermute","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5621_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T20:39:33-07:00","id":1073539,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I don't remember that many side systems. Psi definitely needed to be less underwhelming though, especially for certain groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T16:23:05-07:00","id":1073922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/306030-necro-what-did-the-original-trinity-lines-get-wrong-and-what-did-they-get-right?p=1073539#post1073539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I don't remember that many side systems. Psi definitely needed to be less underwhelming though, especially for certain groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was never fond of the inability to buy powers from other psions either, myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T19:41:15-07:00","id":1073987,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with that. I like having a certain amount of specialty as far as things go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T23:44:46-07:00","id":1074033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/306030-necro-what-did-the-original-trinity-lines-get-wrong-and-what-did-they-get-right?p=1073987#post1073987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fine with that. I like having a certain amount of specialty as far as things go.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with specializing. &quot;Nothing can be higher than your primary mode&quot; would be fine with me. &quot;No more than one dot&quot; was super lame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T10:47:00-07:00","id":1075176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/306030-necro-what-did-the-original-trinity-lines-get-wrong-and-what-did-they-get-right?p=1073539#post1073539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I don't remember that many side systems. Psi definitely needed to be less underwhelming though, especially for certain groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ship to ship combat and the hacking rules are two of the first that I think of. They're not terrible, and they work. But they could've done so much cooler things with them. ^^<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm nitpicking. Love the game overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5621-wintermute","name":"Wintermute","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5621_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T21:43:29-07:00","id":1075361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/306030-necro-what-did-the-original-trinity-lines-get-wrong-and-what-did-they-get-right?p=1074033#post1074033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm fine with specializing. &quot;Nothing can be higher than your primary mode&quot; would be fine with me. &quot;No more than one dot&quot; was super lame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I don't know if the problem was not being able to go outside so much as having such a limited supply of potential powers within your own aptitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T00:47:17-07:00","id":1075397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/306030-necro-what-did-the-original-trinity-lines-get-wrong-and-what-did-they-get-right?p=1075361#post1075361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I don't know if the problem was not being able to go outside so much as having such a limited supply of potential powers within your own aptitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say both. But I definitely want to be able to buy out-of-clan disciplines, so to speak :P Even if it's hard or expensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:18:12-07:00","id":1076144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-